From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:10:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: read_opt: fewer firmware reads per pump pass

#167 makes ~150 firmware reads per pump pass in Dota default mode (64 per
Work at 0.43 passes/Work), against ~90 with #149's knobs, and with
maintenance on each read costs a civac + dsb. read_opt=1 (default,
runtime debugfs asahi_m4/read_opt; 0 restores #167):
- admission keeps each lane's last (read, done) cursors and rereads
  them only when they show no room; cursors only advance, so a stale view
  underestimates room;
- retirement reads the shared render-notifier count through the scan
  snapshot;
- dep_elide's already-reached test uses the previous retire scan's values
  (heap-held; Bootstrap stays small on the probe stack) and keeps the
  item when the stamp was not seen, without reading.
With profile=1, publish_profile now also attributes reads to the event
ring, the retire scan, admission cursors and dep_elide.

Folded in:
- WIP drm/asahi: G16 read_opt: fewer firmware reads per pass, with read-site attribution
- WIP drm/asahi: G16 read_opt: sample wedge detection at most every 50 ms

[WIP drm/asahi: G16 read_opt: sample wedge detection at most every 50 ms]
Read attribution on #168 (Dota default mode, profile=1): of ~60 firmware
reads per Work, ~46 came from check_wedge, which ran at the end of every
retire call that retired nothing, i.e. once per pump pass. Each sample
reads both stamps of every outstanding render flight (plus dependency
stamps) and 36 channel registers. Wedge detection only needs a few
samples per wedge_ms window (default 2 s); with read_opt it samples at
most every 50 ms. Attributed as 'reads: wedge check'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
